; dungeonrefuse.eval — deleting a dungeon (W10), asked of the REAL content.
;
; Nothing here deletes anything: `dungeons what` answers whether a delete would
; be allowed and what it would take, without doing it. The demo's two dungeons
; each meet a different rule first — the crypt is where the game begins, the
; proving ground is where `reset` puts the party — and once the opening is
; moved to the world map, the crypt's two DOORWAYS are what stand in the way.
;
; It also makes the scratch world the next run opens (WorldTest removes it).
logecho on
reset
dungeons
dungeons what crypt
dungeons what eval
dungeons what nosuch
worlds new wt_dng
; In memory only, and restored by WorldTest besides: nothing here saves.
worldprops opening world
dungeons what crypt
